### Quick Checklist Before Launch

1. ✅ All core pages (Home, Category, Product, Cart, Checkout, Account) are functional.  
2. ✅ Responsive design works on mobile, tablet, desktop.  
3. ✅ Images are optimized; lazy‑loaded where appropriate.  
4. ✅ SEO meta tags & structured data added.  
5. ✅ Payment flow tested with test cards.  
6. ✅ Auth flows (login, logout, protected routes) work.  
7. ✅ Cart persists across sessions (localStorage or backend).  
8. ✅ Unit & E2E tests pass.  
9. ✅ Lighthouse score > 90 (performance, accessibility, best practices).  
10. ✅ Deployment pipeline set up (CI/CD).  

---

## 🎉 Final Thought

Building a frontend for an e‑commerce site is a marathon, not a sprint. Start small—get a single product page working, then iterate. Leverage the ecosystem (Next.js, Tailwind, Stripe, Auth0) to reduce boilerplate, focus on the unique value of your store, and keep the user experience smooth and secure.

Happy coding! 🚀
